<title>CANADA: Canada Feb natural gas production rises 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada Feb natural gas production rises 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Tuesday issued the following data for crude oil and natural gas production and exports:</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL AND EQUIVALENT HYDROCARBONS (thousand cubic meters)</p>
<p>		    Feb 1997     Feb 1996	 pct</p>
<p>   Production   9,104.6	9,139.8	 -0.4</p>
<p>   Exports	5,072.4	4,604.5	+10.2</p>
<p>   Imports	3,193.3	3,385.9	 -5.7</p>
<p>   Ref receipts 7,332.6	7,700.0	 -4.8</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (millions of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		   Feb 1997     Feb 1996	  pct</p>
<p>   Production  12,582.7     12,380.9	 +1.6</p>
<p>   Exports	6,893.6	6,469.8	 +6.6</p>
<p>   Canada sales 7,306.3	7,325.1	 -0.3</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL (thousands of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		   Jan/Feb 1997  Jan/Feb 1996   pct</p>
<p>   Production     19,125.4   18,860.9	 1.4</p>
<p>   Exports	  10,984.6   10,479.7	 4.8</p>
<p>   Imports	   7,053.5    6,624.8	 6.5</p>
<p>   Ref receipts   15,807.1   15,376.1	 2.8</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (milions of Cubic meters)</p>
<p>   Production     26,817.3   26,220.2	 2.3</p>
<p>   Exports	  14,339.3   13,616.1	 5.3</p>
<p>   Canada sales   15,831.1   16,067.3	-1.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Canada sales include direct sales.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Gerard O'Connor, Energy Section, (613) 951-3562.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
